t\": \"HAYNES® alloys, because of their creep resistance coupled with oxidation resistance, are ideal for tubes in the really hot spots of industrial furnaces.\", \"position\": 9 }, { \"title\": \"Elastic Modulus of Aluminum\", \"link\": \"https://yajialuminum.com/elastic-modulus-of-aluminum/\", \"snippet\": \"Aluminum has an elastic modulus of approximately 70 GPa (10,000 ksi), but this value varies depending on the alloy. For example, common alloys ...\", \"date\": \"Oct 24, 2025\", \"position\": 10 } ] } ``` * **Analysis:** The search results identified \"Aluminum 6061-T91\" as having a modulus of elasticity of 10,000 ksi, which is at the lower end of the desired range. This provided a specific alloy to investigate further. **Step 2: Focused Search for Annealing Temperature** The next step was to determine the annealing temperature of the candidate alloy, Aluminum 6061, to see if it met the second criterion. * **Tool Used:** `tool-searching.google_search` * **Query:** `\"annealing temperature of Aluminum 6061\"` * **Result:** ```json { \"searchParameters\": { \"q\": \"annealing temperature of Aluminum 6061\", \"gl\": \"us\", \"hl\": \"en\", \"type\": \"search\", \"num\": 10, \"autocorrect\": false, \"page\": 1, \"engine\": \"google\" }, \"answerBox\": { \"snippet\": \"Annealing should be done at 775°F for at 2 to 3 hours at temperature, followed by controlled cooling at 50°F per hour down to 500°F then air cooled. The aging precipitation heat treatment is done at 350°F for 8 hours followed by air cooling. This produces the T6 temper.\", \"snippetHighlighted\": [ \"775°F\" ], \"title\": \"Speedy Metals Information for 6061-T651 Wrought Aluminum Plate\", \"link\": \"https://www.speedymetals.com/information/material6.html\" }, \"organic\": [ { \"title\": \"What Is the Aluminum Annealing Temperature for Aluminium 6061?\", \"link\": \"https://sinoextrud.com/what-is-the-aluminum-annealing-temperature-for-aluminium-6061/\", \"snippet\": \"The ideal annealing temperature for 6061 aluminum is around 775°F (415°C), held for 2–3 hours, followed by controlled furnace cooling.\", \"date\": \"Jul 14, 2025\", \"position\": 1 }, { \"title\": \"How to Anneal Aluminum: The Beginner's Guide - Make It From Metal\", \"link\": \"https://makeitfrommetal.com/how-to-anneal-aluminum-the-beginners-guide/\", \"snippet\": \"Anneal at 650 F then air cool. 6061, Anneal at 775 F, hold for 2-3 hours at temperature, then air cool. 7075, Anneal at 775 F ...\", \"position\": 6 } ] } ``` * **Analysis:** The search results confirmed that the annealing temperature for Aluminum 6061 is approximately 775°F, which is equivalent to 415°C. This temperature falls within the required range of 300°C to 800°C. ### Final Answer Based on the information gathered, **Aluminum 6061** is an alloy that meets the specified criteria. **Detailed Supporting Information:** * **Modulus of Elasticity:** * **Value:** 10,000 ksi * **Fits Criteria:** This value is within the requested range of 10,000 ksi to 18,000 ksi. * **Source:** According to the \"Aluminum 6061-T91 - ASM Material Data Sheet\" from MatWeb, the modulus of elasticity is 10,000 ksi (69 GPa). * **Annealing Temperature:** * **Value:** Approximately 415°C (775°F) * **Fits Criteria:** This value is within the requested range of 300°C to 800°C. * **Source:** Multiple sources confirm this temperature. For instance, Sino Extrud states, \"The ideal annealing temperature for 6061 aluminum is around 775°F (415°C), held for 2–3 hours, followed by controlled furnace cooling.\""
